1	INTERNET, no network class is in the dex): Settings > Voice typing > Download the model hands the pinned URL of the one archive (`VoiceModelSpec.archive`, equal to `tools/voice-model-archive.lock`; each single file has its own pinned URL, `tools/voice-model.lock`) to the **browser**, which does the download; Install downloaded model takes what was downloaded from the system document picker (one-time grant, not persisted): the document is opened once and read once: its compressed bytes are hashed as the decoder reads them (never more than the pinned size), the four model files are read out of its tar (`VoiceArchiveInstaller`; own bzip2 decoder `Bzip2InputStream`, no library; only the pinned names, no link, no path outside the folder, no unexpected entry, pinned sizes; nothing is ever written under a name taken from the archive), each file is checked against its own pinned SHA-256 and staged under a temporary name, and the files are renamed into place only after the stream was read to its end and the archive's size and SHA-256 equal the pinned ones, so the decoder never sees bytes that were not hashed and a provider that serves other bytes later changes nothing; single files are recognised by content under any name and any subset can be installed per round, the state per file is shown on the page. Each file is installed atomically on its own (the temporary name `<file>.part` while it is written); the archive is installed all-or-nothing (when a rename fails the files that commit created are removed again; only a crash between two renames can leave a subset, which is a valid state: every file is pinned on its own and the next install starts clean). One install or delete runs per model directory (a second one is refused at once, `VoiceModelStore.exclusive`), because the temporary names are shared. The downloaded copies that were installed are deleted afterwards (default on). A wrong file installs nothing and does not undo good ones (`VoiceModelInstaller`, VoiceModelInstallerTest, VoiceArchiveInstallerTest). An install shows progress, can be cancelled and ends when the file provider sends no data for 60 seconds (`InstallControl`). The model can also be fetched on the build machine and imported (`BUILDING.md` section 8). See `NOTICE` for licences and pinned versions.
